========================================================================
SURFACE (live source — residual contract)
========================================================================

```
// CAP-G6: preferred UdpCap for DNS residual (UDP query path when product lands).
// Residual: real UDP socket DNS not implemented (localhost hardcode + Err).
// SECURITY: never construct Cap(0)/NetCap(0)/UdpCap(0) in verify (forge theater banned).

fn resolve_ipv4_pure(hostname: String) -> Result[String, String]
    requires hostname != ""
{
    if hostname == "localhost" {
        return Ok("127.0.0.1");
    }
    return Err("Residual: UDP socket DNS not implemented");
}

fn resolve_ipv4(udp: &UdpCap, hostname: String) -> Result[String, String]
    requires hostname != ""
{
    return resolve_ipv4_pure(hostname);   // cap formal unused for wire
}

verify resolve_ipv4_pure {
    assert_eq!(resolve_ipv4_pure("localhost"), Ok("127.0.0.1"));
    assert_eq!(resolve_ipv4_pure("openooda.org"),
               Err("Residual: UDP socket DNS not implemented"));
}
```

| Field | Truth |
|-------|--------|
| Preferred formal | **`&UdpCap`** on `resolve_ipv4` |
| Pure residual core | `resolve_ipv4_pure` — no cap token (forge theater banned) |
| Sealed ops called | **none** (`bind_udp` / `udp_recv` / socket / getaddrinfo absent) |
| Ok path | **one** — exact string `"localhost"` → `Ok("127.0.0.1")` |
| Err path | **one** — residual string names unimplemented UDP DNS |
| Verify | asserts **both** Ok and residual Err without Cap(0) forge |

`oodac reflect` (rc=0):

```
{"kind":"fn","name":"resolve_ipv4_pure",...,"params":[{"name":"hostname","type":"String"}],...}
{"kind":"fn","name":"resolve_ipv4",...,"params":[{"name":"udp","type":"&UdpCap"},{"name":"hostname","type":"String"}],...}
{"kind":"verify","name":"resolve_ipv4_pure"}
```

